{"type":"text","timestamp":1794385916966,"sessionID":"ses_e364b2c5fffeewyZdGbyeKVnGO","part":{"id":"prt_1c9bc340f001vfS5XN0oRN5biX","messageID":"msg_1c9bc21de001g2ksBso2i4m0DP","sessionID":"ses_e364b2c5fffeewyZdGbyeKVnGO","type":"text","text":"<think>expat imports fine in the venv. So the error \"No module named 'expat'\" must come from something else... Perhaps it's from `werkzeug`/`flask`? No. Let me look at the full server log.\n\nAh wait — gunicorn's `--pythonpath backend` and `--chdir /workspace`: I passed `--chdir /workspace` after `--pythonpath backend`, so the relative path \"backend\" resolved relative to... the chdir happens first, so it should be fine. Hmm, but maybe `--chdir` applies before path resolution → `--pythonpath backend` resolves to /workspace/backend → OK.\n\nThe error \"No module named 'expat'\" — hmm! Maybe it's from `xml.parsers.expat`... no, that works.\n\nWait: could it be that gunicorn's worker imports the app from a different Python? No.\n\nLet me see the full log.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794385916943,"end":1794385916962}}}
