{"type":"text","timestamp":1794386183409,"sessionID":"ses_e364b2c5fffeewyZdGbyeKVnGO","part":{"id":"prt_1c9c044d1001Ra3Hs4vxoLbexD","messageID":"msg_1c9c02c39001ktCqCpN0SD32nx","sessionID":"ses_e364b2c5fffeewyZdGbyeKVnGO","type":"text","text":"<think>TypeScript latest is 7.0.2?! Interesting (TS 7 in this future timeline). Let me use typescript@5.9.3 — wait, does 5.9.3 exist? The npm registry here might have TS 7 as latest. Let me check available versions of typescript 5.x.\n\nLet me just install without pinning typescript (use latest = 7.0.2)? TS 7 (the native port) should work for typechecking. But risky with @vitejs/plugin-react? Not related.\n\nLet me check what versions exist: `npm view typescript versions --json | tail`. Simpler: install `typescript@5` to get the latest 5.x.\n\nLet me do: npm install -D tailwindcss@4.3.5 @tailwindcss/vite@4.3.5 \"typescript@^5\" @types/react@19.3.0 @types/react-dom@19.3.0.\n\nNote: the pkill command timed out (odd - pkill returned no output and the shell hung?). Actually the \"(no output)\" plus timeout suggests pkill killed something and the shell session had issues. Let me be careful with background processes: use `setsid nohup ... &` and redirect all fds.\n\nLet me check if the server is still running.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794386183377,"end":1794386183405}}}
